-- A terminal program draws a screen and reads keys.
--
-- The design is Notty's drawing algebra with the size in the type and brick's model-update-view above it: a frame is a value of `Image(w, h)`, built by joining smaller images whose sizes the type checks, and a program is a `Tui` record the loop drives. Nothing here is a command to a screen — `Image` is data, `Tui/render` turns two of them into the bytes that carry one to the other, and only `Tui/Session` touches the terminal.
--
-- **The size is in the type because that is the class of bug this library exists to remove.** A column that does not fill its pane, a widget that overflows it, a border off by one: every surveyed library's issue tracker is full of them, and the two that are honest about it — Notty and brick — pad the mismatch away silently. Here `beside` and `above` refuse a mismatched join where it is written, `view` must produce exactly the frame it was asked for, and the renderer's diff walks two images of one type with no bound to check. The cost is one coercion, `Tui/Image/fit`, wherever a runtime-sized value meets a typed one.
use /std/{Str};

pub mod Color;
pub use Color/{let Color};

pub mod Style;
pub use Style/{let Style};

